        {
          "path": "_m/w/0/z/q/fort-cornwallis-wp/cannon-bases-now-serve-as-benc.jpg",
          "filename": "Cannon bases now serve as benches (12272586526).jpg",
          "caption": "Old cannon wheels serve as benches for seating for visitors. Frankly, it took quite a while for it to register as to what those wheels are, placed randomly near the entrance. I thoughthis had something to do with the fortifications as well. It's only upon reviewing the photos later on, on my computer that I realized that these are old cannon wheels modified as benches. (Georgetown, Penang, Malaysia, Nov. 2013)",
          "alt": "Old cannon wheels serve as benches for seating for visitors. Frankly, it took quite a while for it to register as to what those wheels are, placed randomly near the entrance. I thoughthis had something to do with the fortifications as well. It's only upon reviewing the photos later on, on my computer that I realized that these are old cannon wheels modified as benches. (Georgetown, Penang, Malaysia, Nov. 2013)",
          "width": 4288,
          "height": 2848,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY 2.0",
          "artist": "shankar s. from Dubai, united arab emirates",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cannon_bases_now_serve_as_benches_(12272586526).jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
          "sourceArticleId": "fort-cornwallis-wp",
          "sourceGeohash4": "w0zq",
          "mediumPath": "_m/w/0/z/q/fort-cornwallis-wp/cannon-bases-now-serve-as-benc-medium.webp",
          "smallPath": "_m/w/0/z/q/fort-cornwallis-wp/cannon-bases-now-serve-as-benc-small.webp"
        },
        {
          "path": "_m/w/0/z/q/fort-cornwallis-wp/a-large-cannon-points-to-the-o.jpg",
          "filename": "A large cannon points to the open sea (12272111493).jpg",
          "caption": "And here is another cannon (oh, why do I keep spelling it a 'canon'?!) pointing out to the open sea. It will hit mainland Malaysia if fired. Scores of cannons were confiscated from troops trying to defy the British empire and were placed inside Fort Cornwallis. I'm not sure if this is the same one, but one of the cannons in Fort Cornwallis is called Sri Ramba.i. This is a brass cannon with an interesting history. According to local folks the cannon possess magical powers in which if a lady place a flowers on the barrel of the cannon, her fertility rate will increase. (Georgetown, Penang, Malaysia, Nov. 2013)",
          "alt": "And here is another cannon (oh, why do I keep spelling it a 'canon'?!) pointing out to the open sea. It will hit mainland Malaysia if fired. Scores of cannons were confiscated from troops trying to defy the British empire and were placed inside Fort Cornwallis. I'm not sure if this is the same one, but one of the cannons in Fort Cornwallis is called Sri Ramba.i. This is a brass cannon with an interesting history. According to local folks the cannon possess magical powers in which if a lady place a flowers on the barrel of the cannon, her fertility rate will increase. (Georgetown, Penang, Malaysia, Nov. 2013)",
          "width": 4288,
          "height": 2848,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY 2.0",
          "artist": "shankar s. from Dubai, united arab emirates",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_large_cannon_points_to_the_open_sea_(12272111493).jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
          "sourceArticleId": "fort-cornwallis-wp",
          "sourceGeohash4": "w0zq",
          "mediumPath": "_m/w/0/z/q/fort-cornwallis-wp/a-large-cannon-points-to-the-o-medium.webp",
          "smallPath": "_m/w/0/z/q/fort-cornwallis-wp/a-large-cannon-points-to-the-o-small.webp"
        },
        {
          "path": "_m/w/0/z/q/fort-cornwallis-wp/barracks-ammo-store-in-fort-co.jpg",
          "filename": "Barracks ammo store in Fort Cornwallis (12272000645).jpg",
          "caption": "This was the solitary structure on the fort wall. From the shape of it, I assumed it to be a magazing (gunpowder storage room) or barracks of some sort, which it probably isn't considering that there are no windows on it. A store or magazine seems more like it. (Georgetown, Penang, Malaysia, Nov. 2013)",
          "alt": "This was the solitary structure on the fort wall. From the shape of it, I assumed it to be a magazing (gunpowder storage room) or barracks of some sort, which it probably isn't considering that there are no windows on it. A store or magazine seems more like it. (Georgetown, Penang, Malaysia, Nov. 2013)",
